FILEDEMO - write a small report to the card, then read it back.

Language features
  - <stdio.h> file access from a seed: fopen / fprintf / fgets / fclose
  - the SD card as ordinary C FILEs

Try it
  SEED h%, "FILEDEMO.SED"
    PRINT CALL(h%, 5)   REM write 5 rows to SEEDLOG.TXT, return rows read back

Build it on the machine
  grow filedemo          # -> build/FILEDEMO.SED
  (grow links the berry-libc from SEEDCORE.PKT for this one automatically)
It is also prebuilt in /SEED as FILEDEMO.SED, ready to use.

